---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LoopInstrument from '../components/LoopInstrument.astro';
import { TIERS, TIER_ORDER } from '../lib/tiers';
import { PRODUCTS } from '../lib/products';

const protocols = await getCollection('protocols');
const nodes = await getCollection('nodes');
const releases = await getCollection('releases');

const counts = Object.fromEntries(
  TIER_ORDER.map((t) => [
    t,
    // The gateway-mode entry stands for nine protocols, so count what it lists.
    protocols
      .filter((p) => p.data.verification === t)
      .reduce((n, p) => n + (t === 'gateway-mode' ? p.data.aka.length : 1), 0),
  ]),
) as Record<string, number>;

const newest = (product: string) =>
  releases
    .filter((r) => r.data.product === product)
    .sort((a, b) => b.data.date.getTime() - a.data.date.getTime() || b.data.version.localeCompare(a.data.version, undefined, { numeric: true }))[0];
const gw = newest('gateway');
const gwOut = releases.filter((r) => r.data.product === 'gateway' && r.data.published).sort((a, b) => b.data.version.localeCompare(a.data.version, undefined, { numeric: true }))[0];
const fl = newest('flow');

const fmt = (d: Date) =>
  d.toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' });
---

<Base
  title="HotLoop: automation loops for the real world"
  description="HotLoop closes the loop between what a sensor says and what a machine does: IoT, Edge, Gateway and Edge Relay from one codebase, and Flow, a flow engine."
  ogAlt="HotLoop. Automation loops for the real world."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap-wide grid-hero">
      <div class="copy stack">
        <span class="chip ok">Gateway {gwOut.data.version} is out</span>
        <h1>Automation loops for the real world.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Home automation is a toy right up until the day it matters. Industrial automation works, costs a fortune,
          and comes with a guy who has to drive out to change a setpoint. HotLoop is the thing in the middle that
          should have existed ten years ago: it reads real equipment, keeps the history, raises the alarm and moves
          the machine, from a Pi on a shelf to a whole plant. It's free for you, and free for your business through
          EmberNET.
        </p>
        <div class="cluster">
          <a class="btn primary" href="/gateway/">
            Meet the Gateway
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6" /></svg>
          </a>
          <a class="btn" href="/products/">See the lineup</a>
          <a class="btn" href="/flow/">Meet Flow</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <LoopInstrument />
    </div>

    <div class="wrap-wide stats">
      <div class="stat">
        <div class="n mono">7</div>
        <p>Protocols the Gateway speaks natively. No placeholder drivers, and a table that admits which ones have never met a real PLC.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stat">
        <div class="n mono">{nodes.length}</div>
        <p>Node types in Flow. Each one says how close it is to Node-RED, and the build fails if one lies about it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stat">
        <div class="n mono">25.1<small>MB</small></div>
        <p>The whole Flow image. Node-RED's is 717. The caveats are on <a href="/flow/#numbers">the Flow page</a>, because a benchmark without caveats is marketing in a lab coat.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="label">The loop</span>
        <h2>Sense, decide, act, and around again.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          That's the whole product. A rule you set once and pray over is not a loop. A loop is something you can
          walk away from, because it tells you the truth when it can't see and it refuses to do something stupid
          when somebody tells it to.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <article class="card reveal">
          <h3>Sense</h3>
          <p>
            Poll real equipment over real protocols, and keep the quality of every reading, not just the number. A
            failed read is bad, never zero, so a dead sensor doesn't trip every low alarm on the unit and send the
            night shift chasing a tank that's fine.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card reveal">
          <h3>Decide</h3>
          <p>
            ISA-18.2 alarms, including the one homegrown systems forget: the alarm that cleared on its own before
            anybody saw it. It's still on the list at shift change. Rules compile when you save them, so a typo dies
            in the editor, not at 3am halfway through a batch.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card reveal">
          <h3>Act</h3>
          <p>
            Every write, from a person, a rule or an agent, crosses one gate that nothing routes around. Out of range
            is refused, not clamped, and the refusal gets written down. Want to watch it say no?
            {' '}<a href="/gateway/#the-gate">Go try to break it</a>.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="label">The products</span>
        <h2>Four products from one codebase, and Flow beside them.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Every one of the four speaks every protocol, so you pick the one that fits the box, not the one that
          happens to have your driver. Flow is its own thing with its own license, for people who think in wires.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <article class="card product reveal">
          <div class="cluster head"><h3>HotLoop Gateway</h3><span class="chip ok">Version {gwOut.data.version} is out</span></div>
          <p class="what">
            The site brain, and the one you can install today. It polls the equipment, keeps the history, raises the
            alarms, runs the rules and lets agents read the plant over MCP. One static Go binary, non-root, every
            capability dropped.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Seven native protocols, and a verification table that admits which ones have never touched a real PLC.</li>
            <li>Entities on an ISA-95 tree, so the plant has names instead of register addresses.</li>
            <li>One write gate for people, rules and agents, and a row in the audit for every refusal.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="license">Source-available under the HotLoop Community License. Free for individuals, and free for business through EmberNET.</p>
          <a class="btn primary" href="/gateway/">About the Gateway</a>
        </article>

        <article class="card product reveal">
          <div class="cluster head"><h3>HotLoop Flow</h3><span class="chip ok">Version {fl.data.version} is out</span></div>
          <p class="what">
            Node-RED's idea on a runtime that doesn't fall over. Your <code>flows.json</code> runs as it is, every node
            gets its own goroutine, and every inbox has a ceiling, so a chatty sensor can't balloon the pod until the
            kubelet shoots it.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>{nodes.length} node types, each labeled full, partial, divergent or Flow-only, with the difference written down.</li>
            <li>Won't start without authentication, and ships <code>exec</code> disabled. Node-RED ships with the door open.</li>
            <li>Bounded queues, and a race detector that comes back clean on every package.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="license">Apache-2.0. Free for everyone, businesses included, nobody to ask.</p>
          <a class="btn primary" href="/flow/">About Flow</a>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-4 lineup">
        {PRODUCTS.map((p) => (
          <a class="card mini reveal" href={p.href}>
            <div class="cluster head">
              <h3>{p.name.replace('HotLoop ', '')}</h3>
              <span class={`chip ${p.installable ? 'ok' : 'warn'}`}>{p.installable ? 'Install today' : 'Upcoming'}</span>
            </div>
            <p>{p.tagline}</p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="label">What we refuse to fake</span>
        <h2>Every integration says how far it has actually been proven.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Most integration pages are a wall of logos. Ours has four tiers, and the top one is empty on purpose,
          because nothing has earned it yet. You'd rather know that now than at commissioning.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-4 tiers">
        {TIER_ORDER.map((t) => (
          <div class="card tier reveal">
            <div class="cluster head">
              <span class={`chip ${TIERS[t].chip}`}>{TIERS[t].label}</span>
              <span class="count mono">{counts[t]}</span>
            </div>
            <p>{TIERS[t].blurb}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="more"><a class="btn" href="/integrations/">See every integration</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="label">Latest</span>
        <h2>What changed last, and whether you can download it.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <a class="card release reveal" href="/releases/flow/">
          <div class="cluster head">
            <h3>Flow {fl.data.version}</h3><span class="chip ok">Published</span>
          </div>
          <p class="date">{fmt(fl.data.date)}</p>
          <p>{fl.data.summary}</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card release reveal" href="/releases/gateway/">
          <div class="cluster head">
            <h3>Gateway {gw.data.version}</h3><span class={`chip ${gw.data.published ? 'ok' : 'warn'}`}>{gw.data.published ? 'Published' : 'Merged, not published'}</span>
          </div>
          <p class="date">{fmt(gw.data.date)}</p>
          <p>{gw.data.summary}</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="card licensing reveal">
        <div>
          <span class="label">Licensing</span>
          <h2>Two licenses, no keys.</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            Flow is Apache-2.0: run it, fork it, sell it, nobody to ask. IoT, Edge, the Gateway and the Edge Relay
            are free for individuals, and a business signs up for <a href="https://embernet.ai">EmberNET</a>, free,
            and runs them there, free. There's no key to type in and nothing waiting behind a paywall. Want somebody
            else to own the rollout, SLAs and warranty included? That's our Official Systems Integrators,
            {' '}<a href="https://fireballz.ai">Fireball Industries</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a class="btn primary" href="/license/">Which license applies to me?</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: clamp(var(--hl-s7), 6vw, var(--hl-s8)); }
  .grid-hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 620px); gap: clamp(var(--hl-s6), 5vw, var(--hl-s8)); align-items: center; }
  /* Side by side, the copy column gets about 250px at 1024 and the h1 broke
     "Automation" in the middle of the word. Stack until there's room. */
  @media (max-width: 1100px) { .grid-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .copy > .chip { justify-self: start; }
  /* A grid item defaults to min-width:auto, so its widest child sets the column. */
  .grid-hero > * { min-width: 0; }
  .copy h1 { max-width: 14ch; }

  .stats {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 280px), 1fr));
    gap: var(--hl-s5); margin-top: clamp(var(--hl-s7), 6vw, var(--hl-s8));
    padding-top: var(--hl-s6); border-top: 1px solid var(--hl-border);
  }
  .stat .n { font-size: var(--hl-fs-2xl); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.1; }
  .stat .n small { font-size: 0.45em; margin-left: 0.2em; color: var(--hl-ink-soft); font-weight: 700; }
  .stat p { color: var(--hl-ink-soft); font-size: var(--hl-fs-sm); margin-top: var(--hl-s2); max-width: 40ch; }

  .product { display: grid; gap: var(--hl-s4); align-content: start; }
  .product .head { justify-content: space-between; }
  .product .head h3 { margin: 0; }
  .product .what { color: var(--hl-ink); font-size: var(--hl-fs-base); }
  .product .license { padding-top: var(--hl-s3); border-top: 1px solid var(--hl-border); font-size: var(--hl-fs-xs); }
  .product .btn { justify-self: start; }

  .lineup { margin-top: var(--hl-s5); }
  a.mini { display: grid; gap: var(--hl-s2); align-content: start; text-decoration: none; color: inherit; padding: var(--hl-s5); transition: transform var(--hl-transition-fast), border-color var(--hl-transition-fast); }
  a.mini:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); border-color: var(--hl-orange); }
  .mini .head { justify-content: space-between; }
  .mini h3 { margin: 0; font-size: var(--hl-fs-md); }
  .mini p { font-size: var(--hl-fs-sm); color: var(--hl-ink-soft); }

  .tier .head { justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: var(--hl-s3); }
  .tier .count { font-size: var(--hl-fs-xl); font-weight: 800; }
  .more { margin-top: var(--hl-s6); }

  a.release { display: block; text-decoration: none; color: inherit; transition: transform var(--hl-transition-fast), box-shadow var(--hl-transition-fast), border-color var(--hl-transition-fast); }
  a.release:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); box-shadow: var(--hl-sh-2); border-color: var(--hl-orange); }
  .release .head { justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: var(--hl-s1); }
  .release .head h3 { margin: 0; }
  .release .date { font-size: var(--hl-fs-xs); margin-bottom: var(--hl-s3); }

  .licensing { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--hl-s6); align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; padding: clamp(var(--hl-s6), 5vw, var(--hl-s8)); }
  .licensing > div { display: grid; gap: var(--hl-s3); max-width: 60ch; }
  .licensing .lede { font-size: var(--hl-fs-md); }
</style>
